# Shell scripts run under bash (WSL, Git Bash, Linux, macOS), which rejects CRLF
# line endings. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would convert them and
# every `bash bench/*.sh` would fail on `$'\r'`. The index already holds LF for all
# of them; this only fixes how they are checked out.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Test vectors and reference decodes are raw bytes. A reference YUV with no NUL
# byte looks like text to git, and an autocrlf checkout would then rewrite its
# 0x0A bytes and break the byte-exact comparison.
*.264 binary
*.yuv binary
